 "implication": "A 3% error in most rod parameters (mu, k_bend, aniso, lat_mass, k_stretch) moves the open-loop landing point by several cm (median) and tens of cm (p90), comparable to the 0.10 m target radius, and drops open-loop success from nominal to ~0.3-0.6; 10% errors drop it to 0-0.5. Drag terms (c_visc, c_quad) and the servo matter little. Measured open-loop fidelity (fidelity.json) is far worse than 3% parameter error implies, so an open-loop throw cannot be trusted; the task demands either ~1% model accuracy over 1-3 s or feedback.",
